            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A rectangular fish tank is 50 cm long, 30 cm wide, and 40 cm high (no lid). Find its surface area.</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake:</span> 9,400 cm² (calculated with a lid)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Answer:</span> 2×(50×30+50×40+30×40)−50×30=9,400−1,500=7,900 cm²
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap Analysis:</span> T1+T4 No lid, so subtract the top face; unit conversion cm²→m²
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
