            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A rectangular glass tank is 6 dm long, 5 dm wide, and 4 dm high, with water depth 3.2 dm. A cube with edge length 4 dm is placed into it. How much water overflows?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake:</span> The cube's volume = 64L, all overflows
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Answer:</span> Empty space = 6×5×0.8=24dm³, 64−24=40dm³ overflows (=40L)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap Analysis:</span> T1+T3+T4 Only the water that exceeds the capacity overflows
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
