                <div class="lf-trap-q">A rectangular prism with a base area of 256 cm² is filled with water to a depth of 8 cm. A cube with edge length 8 cm is placed in it. How much does the water level rise?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake:</span> 8/256≈0.03cm
                </div>
                <div class="trap-correct">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Answer:</span> 512÷256=2cm (cube volume ÷ base area = rise in height)
                </div>
                <div class="trap-tip">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Trap Analysis:</span> T1 Water level rise = volume of submerged object ÷ base area of container
                </div>

            </div>
